2026-05-13: trivially fixable.

`haveValidTime()` already exists at line 146 (`return time(nullptr) > 1609459200`, valid after 2021-01-01). Used in drawClock (line 252) and purgeOldLogsIfNeeded (line 399), but NOT in publishAndLog.

Two-line fix in publishAndLog (line 534):
  if (!haveValidTime()) {
    showScanBanner(false, "NTP not ready — retry shortly");
    beepFail();
    return;
  }

(Or: refuse with a more obvious red-screen + log to SD with a flag so we can recover later, but the simple refuse-and-retry is cleanest.)

Pre-tap NTP check at boot already happens (drawClock placeholder "Syncing time…"). The bug is that publishAndLog accepts a tap during that placeholder window if a card is presented before NTP completes.

Belt-and-braces: bridge could reject any payload with ts < 2024-01-01 -> drop into outbox_dead with a clear "pre-NTP" error so we see them later. Not blocking — pairs.

Blocked by hc4.10.
2026-05-14: SHIPPED in firmware v0.7.3.

Two-line guard at start of publishAndLog():
  if (!haveValidTime()) {
    showScanBanner(false, "Clock not set — retry");
    beepFail();
    return;
  }

Tap is dropped (not SD-logged, not pending-queued) rather than stamped
with a wall-clock-zero / 1999 ts. User sees "Clock not set — retry"
banner + fail beep — they re-tap once the boot "Syncing time…"
placeholder clears.

Bridge-side belt-and-braces (reject < 2024-01-01 -> dead-letter) NOT
done. Lower priority now since reader-side guard is the real fix and
nothing else publishes to carrwood/timecard.
